# Docker build context filter for Backend/Dockerfile.
#
# The context is the Backend/ directory (render.yaml sets `rootDir: Backend`), so anything
# outside it — Frontend/, .local-run/, the repository .git/ — is already out of scope and does
# not need a rule here. What follows is only about what lives under Backend/.
#
# MEASURED on 2026-08-11 against this tree with a probe image (`FROM busybox; COPY . /ctx`):
#     no rules at all      1,570,240 KB   (1.45 GB, 60 s to transfer)
#     with these rules       144,040 KB   (144 MB, 14 s)
# The bin/ and obj/ rules account for most of that reduction. On 2026-08-26 the superseded
# Migrations/ estate was also excluded, removing another 95 MB; the tracked context is now about
# 68 MB. See the build-memory record in Dockerfile for the independent compiler-RAM controls.

# === .NET build output — the bulk of it ===
# 1,284 MB on a developer machine that has built both configurations. None of it is build input:
# `dotnet restore` + `dotnet publish` inside the image regenerate everything.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/*.user

# === Not compiled into the image ===
# ERP_RFQ_Automation.Tests is not in the publish graph and pulls Testcontainers, SQLite and the
# xunit runner behind it.
ERP_RFQ_Automation.Tests/
# ERP_RFQ_Automation.AcceptanceFixture is a standalone console harness. It is NOT in
# ERP_RFQ_Automation.sln, no script or workflow references it, and nothing in the Dockerfile
# builds it — it only ProjectReferences the app, never the other way round.
ERP_RFQ_Automation.AcceptanceFixture/
**/TestResults/
**/*.trx

# Superseded by MigrationsBaseline/ and explicitly excluded from compilation by the project.
# Dockerfile's migration guard fails the image build when no live Designer file is compiled, so
# this cannot silently swallow the active migration estate if the folders are renamed later.
ERP_RFQ_Automation/Migrations/

# === Test/tool output that lands under Backend/ when a command is run from the wrong place ===
**/node_modules/
**/.local-run/
**/.e2e-run/
**/playwright-report/

# === Secrets and local configuration — must never be layered into an image ===
# appsettings.Local.json needed its own line: Docker's `*` matches a run of characters, so
# `appsettings.*.Local.json` matches appsettings.Foo.Local.json but NOT appsettings.Local.json.
# The root .gitignore covers that filename, so it is a file developers really do create, and
# without this line it was being copied into the build stage.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/secrets.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pfx
**/*.pem

# === Runtime-written content, not source ===
# The app writes uploaded documents here when it runs outside a container. Tenant data; it has
# no business in an image layer.
ERP_RFQ_Automation/Uploads/

# === OS / editor cruft ===
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — do not "optimise" these without reading why.
#
# ERP_RFQ_Automation/tessdata/  (22 MB)
#   Tesseract loads language data from ContentRootPath/tessdata at RUNTIME and the .csproj
#   copies it to the publish output. Without it OCR fails silently — see the .csproj comment.
#
# ERP_RFQ_Automation/MigrationsBaseline/  (9.3 MB)
#   The live migration estate, plus the .sql files embedded as resources.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
